==English==
[[Image:USS Winston S. Churchill.jpg|thumb|A destroyer (warship)]]

===Etymology===
{{suffix|en|destroy|er}}

The name of the naval vessel is shortened from {{m|en|torpedo boat}} ''destroyer'', the longer term appearing at the end of the 19th century and the shorter form early in the 20th.

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|en|ɔɪ.ə(r)}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun}}

# That which [[destroy]]s something.
# {{lb|en|military}} A small, fast [[warship]] with light [[armament]], smaller than a [[cruiser]], but bigger than a [[frigate]].

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|one who destroys}} {{l|en|devastator}}, {{l|en|decimator}}

